M2Nw==","user":{"login":"hades200082","id":1023581,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMjM1ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1023581?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hades200082","html_url":"https://github.com/hades200082","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hades200082/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hades200082/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hades200082/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hades200082/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hades200082/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hades200082/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hades200082/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hades200082/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hades200082/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2021-06-18T09:58:28Z","updated_at":"2021-06-18T09:58:28Z","body":"@styfle Thanks for suggesting a workaround. Problem is that this would be a pain to have to do literally everywhere I use next/image and needing to wrap next/image in another layer seems to defeat the point of having next/image as a built in component in the first place.\r\n\r\nNext.js provides a loader for Imagix which has a bug in the way it handles image URLs with existing query strings - which is not an uncommon occurrence with CDN image hosting. In fact, with Prismic (which uses Imagix under the hood) their content API returns the Imagix URL's with querystring properties already set in many cases.\r\n\r\nTo improve the developer experience of the next/image component I'd suggest that the built-in loaders need to account for the possibility that the `Src` could already have query string parameters, merging them where possible and overriding them where needed.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://